<topic id="GUID-EE3180E3-2741-4024-95A5-E070B520274F" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>CPU Core Identification</title> 
  <body> 
    <draft-comment>Converted using FMHtml2Dita version: 2.1.0 
    </draft-comment> 
    <p>The CPUID instruction can be used to obtain the processor signatures for CPU core identification. The BIOS must always use the full 32-bit values returned from the CPUID instruction for parsing the processor information. 
    </p> 
    <p><ph>Nova Lake</ph> family processors have Processor Signatures: 
    </p> 
     
    <table id="TABLE_3690B266299640B098ABDA5071615F36"> 
      <tgroup cols="3"> 
        <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*" /> 
        <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="1.43*" /> 
        <colspec colnum="3" colname="col3" colwidth="1.07*" /> 
        <thead> 
          <row> 
            <entry align="center"> 
              <b> Processor Code Name</b> 
            </entry> 
            <entry align="center"> 
              <b> Processor Signature CPUID.(EAX=01h):EAX</b> 
            </entry> 
            <entry align="center"> 
              <b> FMS Encoding</b> 
            </entry> 
          </row></thead> 
        <tbody> 
          <row> 
            <entry> Nova Lake -S/Sx (Desktop) 
            </entry> 
            <entry align="center"> 
              <b> 0x00300F1n</b> 
            </entry> 
            <entry> Processor Family 0x3F, Model 0x01, Stepping n 
            </entry> 
          </row> 
          <row> 
            <entry> Nova Lake -U/P/H/Hx (Mobile) 
            </entry> 
            <entry align="center"> 
              <b> 0x00300F3n</b> 
            </entry> 
            <entry>Processor Family 0x3F, Model 0x03, Stepping n
            </entry> 
          </row> 
        </tbody> 
      </tgroup> 
    </table> 
     
     
     
     
